{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' proof.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Configuration precedence proof\n\n`src/config.mjs` now resolves configuration as `{...defaults, ...local}`. JavaScript keeps the value from the later spread when both objects contain the same key, while keys that are absent from `local` remain from `defaults`.\n\nWith the repository fixtures:\n\n- Defaults: `{\"endpoint\":\"https://default.invalid\",\"timeoutMs\":5000}`\n- Local: `{\"timeoutMs\":2500}`\n- Resolved: `{\"endpoint\":\"https://default.invalid\",\"timeoutMs\":2500}`\n\nTherefore, local `timeoutMs` 2500 overrides default `timeoutMs` 5000, while `endpoint` falls back to its default value, `https://default.invalid`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node test/probe.mjs` exited 0 and printed `precedence-pass`.\n- `git diff --check` exited 0.\n- `LOCAL_NOTES.md` was preserved exactly: its SHA-256 was `498d8cac5af561f8b343266bfb1dbde1376ddd099a455cae156ea5f14925f704` before and after the change, and `git diff --quiet -- LOCAL_NOTES.md` exited 0.\n- The harness-declared `npm run build` and `npm test` could not run because this fixture has no `package.json`; both exited 254 with `ENOENT`.\n- `node scripts/check-harness-map.mjs` could not complete because the harness map references a missing `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`; it exited 1 with `ENOENT`.\n\nThe only project source change is `src/config.mjs`. This proof file is written separately at `$EVALUATION_SUBMISSION/proof.md` as requested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
